# Factory Scaffold & Stage Rules

## Blueprint principles

- The declarative factory config is the source of truth for what gets generated
- Profiles (e.g. light vs overnight) should share the same stage model with different autonomy / stop settings
- Explicit is better than clever: model roles, stop conditions, and review gates should be visible in config

## Stages

Prefer stages with clear contracts:

- Inputs (brief, plan, work order, prior artifacts)
- Outputs (artifacts the next stage can consume)
- Stop conditions / circuit breakers
- Whether a human gate is required

Core line to keep coherent:

1. Plan / interview → product brief
2. Plan → tasks + tests
3. Handoff → packaged work order (planning model → execution model)
4. Loop → build + self-check under stop conditions
5. Review → independent agent grades against original plan and tests
6. Explain → owner’s manual / comprehension update
7. Optional proof / evidence package

Do not invent stages that blur planning, execution, and review into one unsupervised blob.

## Skills & AGENTS.md

- Emit artifacts compatible with common harnesses (Cursor, Claude Code, and similar skill / AGENTS.md conventions)
- AGENTS.md should describe the factory contract, not dump internal Maglio implementation details
- Generated skills should be readable and editable by humans

## Safety rails

- Default scaffolds must include stop conditions
- Review should assume a fresh agent that did not perform the build
- Prefer failing closed when autonomy limits are unclear
- Never encourage “keep going while I sleep” without circuit breakers

## Recipes

- Recipes are shareable stage sets + defaults for a project shape
- Keep recipe format simple enough that others can contribute without deep Maglio internals
- Document assumptions (stack, team size, autonomy level) inside the recipe

## Comprehension

- Prefer generating or updating plain-language owner material when the factory changes behavior
- Evidence packages should answer: what was attempted, what passed, what failed, what was deferred
- Reducing comprehension debt is a feature, not a nice-to-have
